{"availability":"available","full":"BrickerP/BrickerP.github.io","name":"BrickerP.github.io","description":"First-person generative Beijing night drive and personal portfolio on GitHub Pages.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-16T10:55:54Z","updated":"2026-10-10T06:56:51Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://brickerp.github.io/","topics":["beijing","creative-coding","generative-art","github-pages","threejs","typescript","webgl"],"demo":"https://brickerp.github.io/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:08.465Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:08.465Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:08.465Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:04:08.465Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Three.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A seamless first-person night drive through an imagined Beijing. The camera travels at driver-eye height through twelve authored passages in Second-Ring relative order — Tiananmen on the central axis, the palace moat, Shichahai with the white dagoba, Deshengmen, the Second-Ring city threshold, Bell & Drum Towers, Nanluo/Wudaoying, Yonghegong, a CBD/finance skyline, the Temple of Heaven, Qianmen's Dashilar with hutong density, and an overpass return — then arrives back at the same frame every forty-eight seconds.","Artistic composition, not for navigation. This is not a driving aid, road simulation or reconstruction of real streets. The road and city are procedurally authored for the artwork; no commercial tiles, scraped coordinates, live APIs or third-party location services are used.","The runtime derives the full scene from one normalized phase:"],"features":["Stack: Vite · TypeScript · Three.js · plain CSS","View: one first-person drive, with no cockpit or alternate camera mode","Loop: deterministic 48-second closed journey across twelve Beijing passages","Recording: one complete loop exported as WebM when the browser supports it"